## Overview{% #overview %}
The [Datadog MCP Server](https://docs.datadoghq.com/mcp_server/setup.md) enables AI agents to access your Software Delivery data through the [Model Context Protocol (MCP)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/). The `software-delivery` toolset provides tools for interacting with [CI Visibility](https://docs.datadoghq.com/continuous_integration.md), [Test Optimization](https://docs.datadoghq.com/tests.md), [Code Coverage](https://docs.datadoghq.com/code_coverage.md), [DORA metrics](https://docs.datadoghq.com/delivery_performance/dora_metrics.md), and [Deployment Gates](https://docs.datadoghq.com/deployment_gates.md) directly from AI-powered clients like Cursor, Claude Code, or OpenAI Codex.

To use the Software Delivery tools, connect to the Datadog MCP Server with the `software-delivery` toolset enabled. Add the `toolsets` query parameter to the endpoint URL for your [Datadog site](https://docs.datadoghq.com/getting_started/site.md):
```text
https://mcp.<YOUR_DATADOG_SITE>/v1/mcp?toolsets=core,software-delivery
```
For full setup instructions including client configuration for Cursor, Claude Code, VS Code, and other AI clients, see [Set Up the Datadog MCP Server](https://docs.datadoghq.com/mcp_server/setup.md).
